# Trimma button contrast (global — never regress)

**Rule:** Light background → **dark text on all states**. Dark background → **light text on all states** (dark buttons → yellow text on hover).

Use `@/components/ui/button` variants — never one-off button colors.

## Contract

| Fill | Text | Hover text | Hover fill |
|------|------|------------|------------|
| Yellow `#ffde5a` (`variant="default"`) | Black `#000` | Black | Lighter yellow `#ffe680` |
| Black / dark (`variant="dark"`) | White `#fff` | Brand yellow `#ffde5a` | Stay black |

## Implementation

- **Yellow CTAs**: `<Button variant="default">` or `buttonVariants({ variant: "default" })` on links.
- **Dark CTAs**: `<Button variant="dark">` or `trimmaDarkBtnClass` from `@/lib/customer-dashboard-ui`.
- **Filter tabs**: `trimmaFilterTabClass(active)` + `.trimma-filter-tab` CSS — do not invent new tab styles.
- **Semantic tokens**: `:root` is **light** (`--foreground` dark). Dark tokens only under `.dark` or `.trimma-dark-context`.
- **Global safeguards**: `apps/web/src/index.css` block `TRIMMA GLOBAL BUTTON CONTRAST — permanent contract (do not remove)` at file end.

## Do not

- Add `trimma-customer-btn` or page-specific button color classes.
- Put white text on solid yellow buttons or dark text on solid black buttons.
- Override hover to white text on dark buttons (except filter-tab active state).
- Set `:root --foreground` to white (causes white-on-white on light pages).
- Use `hover:text-white` on buttons that hover to `bg-white` / `bg-zinc-50`.
- Use `hover:text-black` / `text-zinc-900` on buttons that hover to `bg-black` / `bg-zinc-900`.

## Mobile

- Interactive controls: minimum **44px** touch height on mobile (`min-h-11` or global `.trimma-customer-dashboard` rules).
- Header CTAs: `w-full sm:w-auto` on narrow viewports.
